 ("pband", "Proportional band is the change in input required to produce a full range of change in the output due to the proportional control action.", PP, 22),
 ("rev", "The proportional controller is reverse-acting so that the control valve throttles down to reduce steam flow as the hot water outlet temperature increases", PP, 25),
 ("wdir", "Direct acting controllers or actuators will respond in the same direction as the control signal", PP, W(CP, "1.17 Process Control Terms")),
 ("int", "Integral control describes a controller in which the output rate of change is dependent on the magnitude of the input.", RS, 28),
 ("intadv", "The major advantage of integral controllers is that they have the unique ability to return the controlled variable back to the exact setpoint following a disturbance.", RS, 32),
 ("intnot", "the integral control mode is not normally used alone, but is combined with another control mode.", RS, 32),
 ("oc", "Output rate of change = Integral constant x % Error", RS, 30),
 ("pi", "It combines the immediate output characteristics of a proportional control mode with the zero residual offset characteristics of the integral mode.", PI2, 34),
 ("wind", "a large sustained error signal will eventually cause the controller to drive to its limit, and the result is called \"reset windup.\"", PI2, 35),
 ("notfreq", "this control mode is not well-suited for processes that are frequently shut down and started up.", PI2, 35),
